Closure decision
Track 5 is GREEN for its approved current canonical scope: an additive universal Auto Tuner/Profile foundation over the proven specialized BlueStacks/Free Fire path. The Track was not scoped to deliver a generic physical tuning runtime for every game. Future game/runtime adapters may consume these contracts without reopening Track 5 by default.

Audit result — no blocking gap
1. Universal search-space candidates contain explicit dimensions/authorities/values only and carry no evidence, validation, recommendation, winner or persistence state.
2. Windows system dimensions enter only through existing explorable Track 2 candidate plans.
3. Workload dimensions require exact adapter authority and reversible capability declarations; generic/unsupported adapters expose no fabricated dimensions.
4. Dynamic BlueStacks/FF candidate correlation remains a one-to-one bridge over the existing specialized generator/runtime and current allow-listed settings.
5. Universal result/winner projections retain exact specialized evidence/profile objects and do not score, validate, select or persist winners.
6. Validated-History projection begins with the existing CanOriginateProfile gate and requires separately measured later validation plus exact configuration/universal-context/candidate correlation.
7. Custom Validated profile provenance requires the existing specialized Custom origin and re-proves exact source/configuration/fingerprint/metrics.
8. Persisted Custom provenance after restart is current-capability reproving; missing capability, ambiguity or drift returns null without weakening specialized validity.
9. AppServices exposes persisted Custom provenance only through an explicit/on-demand seam and adds no startup discovery/provenance work.
10. Profiles presents persisted Custom provenance only from the AppServices result and hides absent provenance.
11. Persisted promoted-winner provenance after restart requires an exact specialized promotion receipt, current persisted winner, preserved Custom, measured revalidation and current Custom universal reproving. It does not reconstruct ProfileChallengeResult or re-evaluate the challenge verdict.
12. AppServices exposes promoted-winner provenance only through an explicit/on-demand seam.
13. Profiles presents promoted-winner provenance in a read-only view, copies only already-proven fields and rejects stale async results.

