Authority invariants preserved at closure
- Observed != Validated.
- Missing capability/evidence/provenance remains absent/Unknown; no invented defaults.
- Stable GameId remains separate from transient PID/path/process evidence.
- Candidate/search-space support is exploration only.
- Existing typed measurement, History validation, ProfileService origin, AutoTunerEngine winner selection and ProfileChallengeService promotion remain specialized authorities.
- Universal layers are correlation/provenance and can only narrow already-authorized specialized state.
- No universal path grants machine mutation or persistence permission.
- Global Controlled Benchmark Lease, Guardian suspension/reconciliation, fingerprint/freshness, rollback and History remain intact.
- Game discovery remains explicit/on-demand and no Track 5 provenance path was added to InitializeAsync().
- WPF remains presentation/request only.

Deferred non-blocking refinements
- Additional game-specific tuning adapters and physical runtimes beyond current proven BlueStacks/FF support.
- Renderer/graphics-option mutation only after a verified reversible lifecycle exists for the exact adapter.
- Generalized persisted provenance for future non-BlueStacks adapters after those adapters possess real measurement/mutation/profile authority.
- Optional batching/caching/polish for current per-profile provenance presentation, preserving freshness semantics.
- Broader DG visual migration remains a later UX track.

Not deferred as hidden debt
The project does not claim that every discovered game is already physically tunable. Unsupported adapters remain capability-honest and expose no fabricated tuning authority.

Exact next action
Track 6 — Adaptive Guardian 2.0 — may now be designed. Before production, inspect the existing Guardian state/session/canary/knowledge paths and define the smallest additive universal Guardian increment. Because Track 6 introduces a new behavioral architecture boundary, require an explicit bounded design approval before its first RED/production cycle.
